# Pairs with EventualConvergence in ReplicationCausalDelivery. With dependencies met by
# identity, merging a write below the origin high-water mark can satisfy a parked
# entry without moving the mark. A drain armed only by an advance never runs for it.
# Production also drains on its maintenance tick, which this design abstracts.
MODULE: EventualConvergenceDrainWakesOnlyOnAdvance
TARGET: EventualConvergence
CLASS: Temporal
SUMMARY: a drain is re-armed only when the high-water mark advances, so an apply below the mark that meets a parked dependency strands the entry
PERTURBS: Deliver
DEADLOCK: off

--- FIND
             /\ wake' = (wake \/ buf # {})
--- REPLACE
\* MUTATION: only an advance re-arms the drain.
             /\ wake' = (wake \/ (w.h > hwm[w.o] /\ buf # {}))
--- END
